{"title":"Career Roadmap: Audit Executive","role":"Audit Executive","summary":"An Audit Executive performs and supports audit activities by examining financial records, testing transactions, reviewing controls, identifying exceptions and preparing audit documentation.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com - Forensic Accounting / Auditing"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build accounting, auditing, forensic investigation, fraud detection, internal-control, compliance and data-analysis skills"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Audit Executive performs and supports audit activities by examining financial records, testing transactions, reviewing controls, identifying exceptions and preparing audit documentation."},{"type":"p","text":"With a Forensic Accounting / Auditing specialization, the student should go beyond conventional financial auditing and develop the ability to investigate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fraud"},{"text":"Financial irregularities"},{"text":"Misappropriation"},{"text":"Suspicious transactions"},{"text":"Revenue manipulation"},{"text":"Vendor fraud"},{"text":"Expense fraud"},{"text":"Asset misuse"},{"text":"Financial-reporting anomalies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The core professional workflow is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Financial Data","Risk Assessment","Audit Testing","Exception Identification","Investigation","Evidence","Documentation","Findings","Recommendation"]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Accounting foundation"},{"text":"Financial accounting, economics, statistics"},{"text":"Accounting case studies"},{"text":"Weak accounting fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Auditing foundation"},{"text":"Audit procedures, controls, taxation"},{"text":"Audit working papers"},{"text":"Treating audit as simple checking"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Forensic capability"},{"text":"Fraud investigation, analytics, evidence"},{"text":"Forensic case study"},{"text":"Making unsupported fraud allegations"}],[{"text":"Final Stage"},{"text":"Industry readiness"},{"text":"Data analytics, ERP, compliance, internship"},{"text":"Audit internship + forensic capstone"},{"text":"No practical investigation experience"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial Accounting"},{"text":"Business Economics"},{"text":"Business Mathematics"},{"text":"Business Communication"},{"text":"Business Law"},{"text":"Excel fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Corporate Accounting"},{"text":"Cost Accounting"},{"text":"Business Statistics"},{"text":"Financial Statement Analysis"},{"text":"Taxation fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Auditing principles"},{"text":"Audit planning"},{"text":"Audit evidence"},{"text":"Internal controls"},{"text":"Audit documentation"},{"text":"Advanced Excel"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Forensic Accounting"},{"text":"Fraud examination"},{"text":"Corporate governance"},{"text":"Risk management"},{"text":"GST fundamentals"},{"text":"Income-tax fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Forensic audit techniques"},{"text":"Fraud-risk assessment"},{"text":"Financial data analytics"},{"text":"IT controls"},{"text":"Cyber-fraud awareness"},{"text":"SQL/Power BI"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 6"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Investigation methodology"},{"text":"Digital evidence fundamentals"},{"text":"Financial crime awareness"},{"text":"Audit analytics"},{"text":"Internship"},{"text":"Forensic audit capstone"}]}]},{"heading":"Accounting Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Transaction","Journal","Ledger","Trial Balance","Adjustments","Financial Statements"]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Assets"},{"text":"Liabilities"},{"text":"Equity"},{"text":"Revenue"},{"text":"Expenses"},{"text":"Receivables"},{"text":"Payables"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Fixed assets"},{"text":"Depreciation"},{"text":"Provisions"},{"text":"Accruals"},{"text":"Borrowings"},{"text":"Tax balances"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A forensic auditor must understand accounting deeply enough to identify transactions that do not make economic or accounting sense."}]},{"heading":"Financial Statement Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"h","text":"Balance Sheet"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Working capital"},{"text":"Debt"},{"text":"Receivables"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Fixed assets"},{"text":"Related-party balances"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Profit & Loss"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unusual revenue growth"},{"text":"Margin changes"},{"text":"Expense anomalies"},{"text":"Unusual provisions"},{"text":"Unusual write-offs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cash Flow"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare:"},{"type":"h","text":"Profit ↔ Operating Cash Flow"},{"type":"p","text":"Large unexplained differences can become an area for further investigation."}]},{"heading":"Audit Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit planning"},{"text":"Risk assessment"},{"text":"Materiality"},{"text":"Audit evidence"},{"text":"Audit procedures"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Analytical procedures"},{"text":"Professional skepticism"},{"text":"Audit documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Audit Framework"},{"type":"flow","items":["Assertion","Risk","Procedure","Evidence","Conclusion"]}]},{"heading":"Audit Assertions","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Existence"},{"text":"Completeness"},{"text":"Occurrence"},{"text":"Accuracy"},{"text":"Cut-off"},{"text":"Classification"},{"text":"Valuation"},{"text":"Rights and obligations"},{"text":"Presentation and disclosure"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"p","text":"If a company reports ₹50 crore of receivables:"},{"type":"p","text":"Ask:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Do the customers actually exist?"},{"text":"Did the sales actually occur?"},{"text":"Are the balances recoverable?"},{"text":"Are there unusual related-party customers?"},{"text":"Are sales recorded in the correct period?"}]}]},{"heading":"Internal Controls","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Control environment"},{"text":"Risk assessment"},{"text":"Control activities"},{"text":"Information & communication"},{"text":"Monitoring"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important controls:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Segregation of duties"},{"text":"Authorization"},{"text":"Maker-checker"},{"text":"Access control"},{"text":"Approval limits"},{"text":"Reconciliation"},{"text":"Physical verification"},{"text":"Audit trails"}]}]},{"heading":"Fraud Risk","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand common fraud categories."},{"type":"h","text":"Asset Misappropriation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cash theft"},{"text":"Inventory theft"},{"text":"Unauthorized payments"},{"text":"Expense reimbursement fraud"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Fraudulent Financial Reporting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fake revenue"},{"text":"Premature revenue recognition"},{"text":"Understated liabilities"},{"text":"Overstated assets"},{"text":"Manipulated expenses"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Corruption"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bribery"},{"text":"Kickbacks"},{"text":"Conflicts of interest"},{"text":"Vendor collusion"}]}]},{"heading":"Forensic Accounting","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how forensic accounting differs from routine auditing."},{"type":"h","text":"Traditional Audit"},{"type":"p","text":"Primarily asks:"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Are the financial statements fairly presented based on applicable requirements?\""},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Investigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Often asks:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"What happened, how did it happen, who/what was involved, what evidence supports the conclusion, and what financial impact resulted?\""},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fraud investigation"},{"text":"Financial reconstruction"},{"text":"Transaction tracing"},{"text":"Asset tracing"},{"text":"Funds-flow analysis"},{"text":"Fraud-risk assessment"},{"text":"Investigative interviewing fundamentals"},{"text":"Evidence documentation"},{"text":"Expert-report concepts"}]}]},{"heading":"Fraud Investigation Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Complaint/Red Flag","Preliminary Assessment","Scope Definition","Data Collection","Analysis","Investigation","Evidence Evaluation","Findings","Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Maintain clear documentation of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Source of data"},{"text":"Analysis performed"},{"text":"Exceptions identified"},{"text":"Supporting evidence"},{"text":"Assumptions"},{"text":"Conclusions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"An auditor should distinguish between:"},{"type":"h","text":"Anomaly ≠ Proof of Fraud"},{"type":"p","text":"An unusual transaction may require investigation but does not automatically establish wrongdoing."}]},{"heading":"Financial Red Flags","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"h","text":"Revenue"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unusual end-of-period sales"},{"text":"Large unexplained sales growth"},{"text":"Round-number transactions"},{"text":"Unusual credit notes"},{"text":"High sales with weak cash collections"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Expenses"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate invoices"},{"text":"Unusual vendors"},{"text":"Round-number expenses"},{"text":"Personal expenses through company accounts"},{"text":"Unusual related-party payments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Vendors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate bank accounts"},{"text":"Shared addresses"},{"text":"Shared contact information"},{"text":"Unusual vendor creation"},{"text":"High-risk payment patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Employees"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate bank accounts"},{"text":"Ghost employees"},{"text":"Unusual overtime"},{"text":"Unusual reimbursements"}]}]},{"heading":"Audit Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to analyze large transaction datasets."},{"type":"h","text":"Tests"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate transactions"},{"text":"Duplicate invoices"},{"text":"Benford's Law as an investigative screening technique"},{"text":"Round-number analysis"},{"text":"Weekend transactions"},{"text":"Holiday transactions"},{"text":"Unusual posting times"},{"text":"Manual journal entries"},{"text":"Sequential invoice gaps"},{"text":"Unusual users"},{"text":"Unusual vendors"},{"text":"Related-party transactions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These are screening techniques, not standalone proof of fraud."}]},{"heading":"Excel for Audit","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"COUNTIFS"},{"text":"IF"},{"text":"IFERROR"},{"text":"ROUND"},{"text":"TEXT"},{"text":"Date functions"},{"text":"PivotTables"},{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"Power Pivot"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use Excel for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reconciliations"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Duplicate testing"},{"text":"Aging"},{"text":"Exception reporting"},{"text":"Journal-entry analysis"},{"text":"Vendor analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"SQL for Forensic Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"HAVING"},{"text":"ORDER BY"},{"text":"CASE"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"Window functions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Queries"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate invoices"},{"text":"Duplicate payments"},{"text":"High-value transactions"},{"text":"Transactions outside business hours"},{"text":"Unusual vendors"},{"text":"Multiple vendors sharing details"},{"text":"Employee/vendor overlaps"}]}]},{"heading":"Python for Forensic Analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Use:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"matplotlib"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to automate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate detection"},{"text":"Transaction filtering"},{"text":"Outlier analysis"},{"text":"Data reconciliation"},{"text":"Vendor clustering"},{"text":"Journal-entry testing"},{"text":"Trend analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Optional advanced skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"scikit-learn"},{"text":"anomaly detection"},{"text":"clustering"},{"text":"network analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"Digital Evidence Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand at a conceptual level:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital evidence"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Audit logs"},{"text":"Email evidence"},{"text":"File timestamps"},{"text":"Access records"},{"text":"Transaction logs"},{"text":"Data preservation"},{"text":"Evidence integrity"},{"text":"Chain of custody"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Forensic accounting professionals should understand when specialist digital-forensics/cybersecurity professionals are required."}]},{"heading":"Cyber-Fraud Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Phishing"},{"text":"Business email compromise"},{"text":"Payment fraud"},{"text":"Account takeover"},{"text":"Identity fraud"},{"text":"Credential theft"},{"text":"Invoice fraud"},{"text":"Social engineering"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how cyber incidents can create financial and accounting consequences."}]},{"heading":"Tax & Compliance","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn fundamentals of:"},{"type":"h","text":"GST"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Input tax credit"},{"text":"Output tax"},{"text":"Invoices"},{"text":"Returns"},{"text":"Reconciliation"},{"text":"Suspicious transactions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Income Tax"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Taxable income"},{"text":"TDS"},{"text":"Tax deductions"},{"text":"Tax compliance"},{"text":"Basic tax investigations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Corporate Compliance"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Companies"},{"text":"Directors"},{"text":"Related-party transactions"},{"text":"Corporate governance"},{"text":"Statutory filings"}]}]},{"heading":"ERP & Accounting Systems","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TallyPrime"},{"text":"SAP"},{"text":"Oracle"},{"text":"Microsoft Dynamics"},{"text":"Zoho Books"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"General Ledger"},{"text":"Accounts Payable"},{"text":"Accounts Receivable"},{"text":"Procurement"},{"text":"Sales"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Fixed Assets"},{"text":"User access"},{"text":"Audit logs"},{"text":"Segregation of duties"}]},{"type":"p","text":"ERP knowledge is important because many forensic investigations begin with large transactional datasets extracted from ERP systems."}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Fraud Detection Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a transaction dataset and identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate invoices"},{"text":"Duplicate payments"},{"text":"Round-number transactions"},{"text":"Unusual transaction times"},{"text":"Unusual vendors"},{"text":"High-value transactions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce an exception report."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Vendor Fraud Investigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze vendor master data for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate vendors"},{"text":"Shared bank accounts"},{"text":"Shared addresses"},{"text":"Shared phone numbers"},{"text":"Unusual payment patterns"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a vendor-risk scoring model."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Journal Entry Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyze general-ledger transactions for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manual entries"},{"text":"Unusual users"},{"text":"Weekend entries"},{"text":"Month-end entries"},{"text":"Round numbers"},{"text":"Unusual accounts"},{"text":"Large adjustments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a Power BI investigation dashboard."}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Audit & Fraud Analytics Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["ERP Data","Data Cleaning","Risk Rules","Anomaly Detection","Investigation Queue","Evidence","Findings","Report"]},{"type":"h","text":"Modules"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Transaction ingestion"},{"text":"Vendor analysis"},{"text":"Customer analysis"},{"text":"Journal-entry testing"},{"text":"Duplicate detection"},{"text":"Anomaly detection"},{"text":"Relationship analysis"},{"text":"Risk scoring"},{"text":"Investigation notes"},{"text":"Evidence register"},{"text":"Power BI dashboard"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Suggested Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"PostgreSQL"},{"text":"ERP data concepts"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Roadmap","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit firms"},{"text":"CA firms"},{"text":"Forensic accounting firms"},{"text":"Internal audit departments"},{"text":"Risk consulting firm